<title>UK: Dixons down after report of OFT probe.</title>
<headline>Dixons down after report of OFT probe.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dixons Plc shares dropped in pre-market trade on Tuesday after a report in the Times said the company could face an enquiry over alledged tactics to have rivals excluded from out-of-town shopping centres.</p>
<p>The paper said the Office of Fair Trading could launch a formal enquiry, after complaints by rivals that the company had used an unfair and anti-competitive strategy to force developers to deny them floorspace.</p>
<p>Shares in the electrical retailer were quoted down 5p at 491, not far from it's year's low of 474p set on February 4, though no trading was recorded in the stock.</p>
</text>
